.TH wc 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
wc \- count lines, words and characters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wc
[\fB\-lwc\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wc
counts lines, words and characters in each
.IR file ,
and prints a total if more than one was named.  With no
.IR file ,
it reads standard input.
.PP
With no options all three counts are printed.  Naming any of
.BR \-l ,
.B \-w
or
.B \-c
selects just those, in the fixed order lines, words, characters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Count lines.  A line is a newline or a formfeed, so an unterminated last
line is not counted.
.TP
.B \-w
Count words: runs of anything that is not whitespace.
.TP
.B \-c
Count characters, which on FUZIX are bytes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# wc prog.c
# wc -l *.bas
# who | wc -l
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cksum (1),
.BR sum (1)
